{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rz6uL7jbsRr28GAQCgi75j","type":"tool_result","content":"85\t   converse, and is *definitionally* the same type read the other way round:\n86\t   `𝑨 ≤ 𝑩` and `𝑩 ≥ 𝑨` both unfold to an injective homomorphism from `𝑨` into\n87\t   `𝑩`.\n88\t+  `mon→≤`{.AgdaFunction} turns a monomorphism into a proof of the subalgebra\n89\t   relation.  It is immediate, because `mon→intohom`{.AgdaFunction} of\n90\t   [Setoid.Homomorphisms.Basic][] already produces exactly this type.\n91\t+  `SubalgebraOf`{.AgdaRecord} bundles both algebras and the proof into a single\n92\t   record.  `Subalgebra`{.AgdaFunction} instead fixes the larger algebra and\n93\t   collects the smaller one with its embedding, so an inhabitant of\n94\t   `Subalgebra 𝑨` is a pair `(𝑩 , p)` with `p : 𝑩 ≤ 𝑨`.\n95\t\n96\t```agda\n97\tmodule _ {𝑆 : Signature 𝓞 𝓥} where\n98\t  _≥_   -- alias for supalgebra (aka overalgebra)\n99\t    _IsSupalgebraOf_ : Algebra {𝑆 = 𝑆} α ρᵃ → Algebra {𝑆 = 𝑆} β ρᵇ → Type (𝓞 ⊔ 𝓥 ⊔ α ⊔ ρᵃ ⊔ β ⊔ ρᵇ)\n100\t  𝑨 IsSupalgebraOf 𝑩 = Σ[ h ∈ hom 𝑩 𝑨 ] IsInjective (proj₁ h)\n101\t\n102\t  _≤_   -- alias for subalgebra relation\n103\t    _IsSubalgebraOf_ : Algebra {𝑆 = 𝑆} α ρᵃ → Algebra {𝑆 = 𝑆} β ρᵇ → Type (𝓞 ⊔ 𝓥 ⊔ α ⊔ ρᵃ ⊔ β ⊔ ρᵇ)\n104\t  𝑨 IsSubalgebraOf 𝑩 = Σ[ h ∈ hom 𝑨 𝑩 ] IsInjective (proj₁ h)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"621d0fec-f3c0-47a9-a2a1-29470c5f746f","uuid":"685530a7-e267-4da5-b5a0-baecc38fe2f8","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:46:45.893Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/nix/store/0mkdwhwzshgsa7xknd81r8hvdp6gbmr6-agda-algebras-unstable-2026-09-07/src/Setoid/Subalgebras/Basic.lagda.md","content":"   converse, and is *definitionally* the same type read the other way round:\n   `𝑨 ≤ 𝑩` and `𝑩 ≥ 𝑨` both unfold to an injective homomorphism from `𝑨` into\n   `𝑩`.\n+  `mon→≤`{.AgdaFunction} turns a monomorphism into a proof of the subalgebra\n   relation.  It is immediate, because `mon→into